# SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000082  -  CAT II
# The web server must allow the mappings to unused and vulnerable scripts to
# be removed.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000082
group:           V-206381
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000381
control_rev5:    CM-7

contribution:    A script mapping in Splunk is a custom search command stanza that binds a
                 command name to a file and an interpreter; the application can show that
                 no mapping still names a retired interpreter version.

governs:         commands.conf - Custom search commands an app provides.

check:           commands.conf [] python.version not_equals python2

external:        Which command mappings the deployment's searches and dashboards still use,
                 carried by the app review procedure; the application cannot tell an unused
                 mapping from a rarely used one.
external:        Removal of the script files themselves from the app directories, carried
                 by the operating system file system.

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000141-WSR-000082 check and fix text;
                 commands.conf.spec:57 (python.version =
                 {default|python|python2|python3|python3.7|python3.9|latest}),
                 commands.conf.spec:68 (filename), commands.conf.spec:53 (type)
finding:         A custom search command mapping still selects the retired python2
                 interpreter, so the application retains a mapping to a script interpreter
                 that is no longer supported.
